event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":93,"item_id":"rs_03ed77a8590895b5016aca79313dcc87d19eb75b5825a2fc05","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering form implementation**\n\nI'm thinking about implementing a server-rendered simple form with fetch. The idea is to make it easy to create and display errors without requiring unnecessary browser JavaScript. So, I could use HTML to handle POST requests for projects and validate through server rendering. It seems like the standard approach with server-rendered forms is ideal, especially if I can leverage HTML with module script for enhanced validation. Tests would also be crucial to verify everything works as intended."}

